=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: mswitch0
diagnosis_text:
**Affected component:** OSPF routing configuration on mswitch0 — ospfd is running but has no `network` statements at all.

**Mechanism:** mswitch0 is the Layer-3 gateway for all three campus 1 PC subnets: it holds `172.16.10.254/24` (VLAN 10), `172.16.20.254/24` (VLAN 20), and `172.16.30.254/24` (VLAN 30) as directly connected interfaces. Because it has zero OSPF configuration, these subnets are never injected into the OSPF domain, so every other router in the topology — including router16, router7, and sshswitch — has no routing entry for any 172.16.x.x prefix. The reverse path fails for the same reason: mswitch0 has no default route and learns no OSPF routes, so when a campus 1 PC sends traffic toward campus 2 (10.5.0.x / 10.6.0.x), mswitch0 itself generates the "Destination Net Unreachable" ICMP (observed from 172.16.10.254). Campus 2 gateways (10.5.0.254, 10.6.0.254 on sshswitch) generate the same ICMP in the opposite direction because the 172.16.x.x subnets are absent from sshswitch's OSPF-learned RIB. Intra-campus-1 traffic still works because mswitch0 routes locally between its own connected VLANs without needing OSPF.

**Localization:** mswitch0, all interfaces — vlan10/vlan20/vlan30 and bond0 (the uplink to router16 at 10.2.2.0/24).

**Root cause:** mswitch0's ospfd process has no OSPF `network` statements configured, leaving it completely isolated from the OSPF routing domain.

**Fix:** Add OSPF area-0 network statements on mswitch0 covering `10.2.2.0/24` (to form an adjacency with router16 and exchange routes), `172.16.10.0/24`, `172.16.20.0/24`, and `172.16.30.0/24` (to advertise the campus 1 subnets to the rest of the OSPF domain).
=== END ===